  "prefLabel": "Plc 1903.04 Information Required for Initial Doula Certification Application",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1903.04 Information Required for Initial Doula Certification Application. In addition to the information required by Plc 304.03, an applicant for initial doula certification shall provide:\n\n(a) If qualifying under Plc 1903.02(b)(1), the name, location, and URL of the certifying organization; or\n\n(b) If qualifying under Plc 1903.02(b)(2):\n\n(1) The name, location, and URL of the school or program that provided the applicant’s doula training;\n\n(2) The city and state of each of the required births the applicant attended in the preceding 5 years; and\n\n(3) The city and state in which the applicant made each of the required visits during the perinatal period in each year after completing training.\n\nSource. #14429, eff 1-16-26, EXPIRES 1-16-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1900.html"
